  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SHAPE-SEA Human Rights Research 2021-2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">SHAPE-SEA Human Rights Research 2021-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mahidol University (Nakhon Pathom, Thailand) in collaboration with ASEAN University Network - Human Rights and Education (AUN-HRE, Nakhon Pathom, Thailand) and Southeast Asian Human Rights Studies Network (SEAHRN, Depok, Indonesia), has applied to Sida for support for a regional research network in the field of human rights and peace studies. The project proposal is entitled: Strengthening human rights and peace research and education in ASEAN / Southeast Asia (SHAPE-SEA): Funding proposal for program phase 2 (July 2021-December 2024). The SHAPE-SEA research network and its activities will be implemented regionally in Southeast Asia, with a special focus on Cambodia, Laos, Vietnam and East Timor, where the research capacity for peace and human rights studies is assessed to require further support.

The SHAPE-SEA Phase 2 contribution will build upon the results achieved during SHAPE-SEA phase 1 (2015 - 2021). The Sida grant will enable the SHAPE-SEA Secretariat at Mahidol University to strengthen research capacity amongst Southeast Asian peace and human rights researchers, and to strengthen respect for academic freedom in Southeast Asia. The grant will also support Southeast Asian peace and human rights researchers to 1) produce new knowledge, 2) engage with regional and national stakeholders to implement research results,  and 3) contribute to public human rights discourses. and peace in Southeast Asia. 

Research scholarships will be awarded to researchers in the region to carry out research projects that study local, national and cross-border research issues related to peace and human rights. The research results and research capacity generated by the initiative will contribute to improved conditions for fair and sustainable development that is inclusive of vulnerable and marginalized groups in Southeast Asia. 

The total budget of the contribution during July 2021 - December 2024 is 16,6 million SEK. Approximately 2,7 million SEK of the funding will be forwarded from Mahidol University to researchers at Southeast Asian universities and research organizations in the form of small scholarships to support research activities.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mahidol universitet (Nakhon Pathom, Thailand) i samarbete med ASEAN University Network - Human Rights and Education (AUN-HRE, Nakhon Pathom, Thailand) och Southeast Asian Human Rights Studies Network (SEAHRN, Depok, Indonesien), har ans&#xF6;kt om st&#xF6;d f&#xF6;r ett regionalt forskningsn&#xE4;tverk inom teman m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter och fred. Projektf&#xF6;rslaget &#xE4;r Strengthening human rights and peace research and education in ASEAN/Southeast Asia (SHAPE-SEA) Phase 2 (July 2021-December 2024). SHAPE-SEA forskningsn&#xE4;tverket och dess verksamhet kommer att arbeta regionalt i Sydostasien, med s&#xE4;rskilt fokus p&#xE5; Kambodja, Laos, Vietnam och &#xD6;st Timor d&#xE4;r forskningskapacitet inom fred och m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter bed&#xF6;ms som i behov av ytterligare st&#xF6;d.

SHAPE-SEA Phase 2 kommer att bygga vidare p&#xE5; resultaten som uppn&#xE5;ddes under SHAPE-SEA Phase 1 (2015-2021). Sida-bidraget g&#xF6;r det m&#xF6;jligt f&#xF6;r SHAPE-SEA sekretariatet vid Mahidol University att st&#xE4;rka forskningskapaciteten bland sydostasiatiska forskare inom freds- och m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttighetsstudier. Projektet kommer ocks&#xE5; att st&#xF6;dja sydostasiatiska forskare att ta fram ny kunskap, samarbeta med regionala och nationella akt&#xF6;rer f&#xF6;r att genomf&#xF6;ra forskningsresultat och bidra till offentliga diskurser om m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter och fred i Sydostasien.

Forskningsstipendier kommer att delas ut till forskare i regionen f&#xF6;r att genomf&#xF6;ra forskningsprojekt som studerar lokala, nationella och gr&#xE4;ns&#xF6;verskridande forskningsfr&#xE5;gor relaterade till fred och m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter. De forskningsresultat och forskningskapacitet som initiativet genererar kommer att bidra till f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttrade f&#xF6;ruts&#xE4;ttningar f&#xF6;r en r&#xE4;ttvis och h&#xE5;llbar utveckling som inkluderar s&#xE5;rbara och marginaliserade grupper i Sydostasien.

Insatsens totala budget under juli 2021 - december 2024 &#xE4;r 16,6 miljoner SEK. Cirka 2,7 miljoner SEK kommer at vidaref&#xF6;rmedlas fr&#xE5;n Mahidol universitet i form av mindre forskningsstipendier till forskare  vid sydostasiatiska universitet och forskningsorganisationer f&#xF6;r forskningsverksamhet.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objectives of SHAPE-SEA Phase 2 are:

- to support and strengthen homegrown academic interest, skills and knowledge on researching human rights and peace in ASEAN/Southeast Asia.

- to create change by enhancing, influencing and translating policies, processes and practices of human rights and peace into action in ASEAN/Southeast Asia

- to ensure excellence in producing, disseminating, and analyzing knowledge on human rights and peace in ASEAN/Southeast Asia

- to further developing ways and means to internalizing human rights and peace knowledge amongst teaching staff, academic leaders and students in Higher Education Institutions in ASEAN/Southeast Asia</narrative>
  </description>
